lose the original geometry. The controls require the same exact glyph,
make no backend request and write no file until the user downloads TSV.

A later non-identity transform replaces history; a zero-change transform
or refused edit preserves earlier undo/redo. Any separate authored edit,
TSV load or session reset invalidates the snapshot. This does not add
persistent named variants or multi-step history; P1-014 remains open.

## Two-row joined accented handwriting acceptance (partial) — 2026-11-04

The repeatable `pnpm run test:joined-ink` subprocess journey now saves
independent exact NFD `a` plus combining acute and NFC `ó` glyphs as a
canonical six-segment Rust TSV library, then flows two authored text rows.

It renders real PDF and transparent PNG with seeded per-occurrence width,
height, slant and endpoint regularity. The PDF has 24 authored segments
plus four explicit physical connectors, two per row; without the selected
NFD-to-NFC join it has exactly 24 segments. Both rows use distinct sheet
